  "linked_issues": [
    {
      "body": "Previously, if `FLASK_ENV` was not set, it would default to `\"production\"`, now it defaults to `\"development\"`.\r\n\r\nReproduction:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nfrom flask import Flask\r\n\r\napp = Flask(__name__)\r\n\r\n@app.route(\"/\")\r\ndef hello_world():\r\n    print(f\"{app.config.get('ENV')=}\")\r\n    return \"<p>Hello, World!</p>\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nRun using gunicorn, `gunicorn flask_demo.app:app` with `FLASK_ENV` unset,\r\n\r\nFlask 2.2.1, this handler prints:\r\n`app.config.get('ENV')='development'`\r\n\r\ndowngrade to 2.1.0:\r\n`app.config.get('ENV')='production'`\r\n\r\nI assume this due to  #4720, `src/flask/app.py:693`\r\n\r\nEnvironment:\r\n\r\n- Python version: 3.10.4\r\n- Flask version: 2.2.1",
      "number": 4740,
      "url": "https://github.com/pallets/flask/issues/4740"
    }
  ],
